WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.938
Let’s walk through Plugins.

00:00:01.938 --> 00:00:05.575
Review plugin scope, dependency state, and selected session

00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:07.888
before changing lifecycle state.

00:00:07.888 --> 00:00:11.162
A plugin must not silently affect another run or become

00:00:11.162 --> 00:00:14.613
a substitute for the platform’s deterministic workflow.

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:17.775
On this slide, review and manage the plugin lifecycle

00:00:17.775 --> 00:00:19.512
for the selected session.

00:00:19.512 --> 00:00:23.613
In practice, confirm scope and dependency state before enabling

00:00:23.613 --> 00:00:25.262
or disabling a plugin;

00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:28.438
a plugin must not silently alter another session.

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:31.585
When you are ready, use Open Plugins to move

00:00:31.585 --> 00:00:33.072
to the live surface.

00:00:33.072 --> 00:00:35.785
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:35.935
.
